      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Calculator\n\nA small offline pixel-style calculator built with plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. No packages, no network requests, no storage.\n\n## Features\n\n- Two number inputs (`left`, `right`) supporting negative and decimal values.\n- Operation selector (`add`, `subtract`, `multiply`, `divide`).\n- Calculate button (`calculate`) and result output (`result`) that starts at `0`.\n- Output shows only the numeric result (or the exact text `Error`).\n- Rejects empty inputs, non-finite numbers, and division by zero with `Error`.\n- Fully keyboard accessible with visible focus, hover and pressed states.\n- Responsive layout that works from 360px wide.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser (double-click works offline).\n2. Enter a left number and a right number.\n3. Choose an operation.\n4. Click **Calculate** or press **Enter**.\n5. The result appears in the output area.\n\n## Error handling\n\nThe result area displays exactly `Error` when:\n\n- Either input is empty or not a finite number (e.g. `abc`, `Infinity`).\n- Division by zero is attempted.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` – structure and required IDs.\n- `style.css` – pixel-art theme and responsive layout.\n- `script.js` – calculation and validation logic.\n- `README.md` – this file.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Offline only: no imports, packages, network requests, external assets, iframes or server code.\n- Uses `addEventListener` instead of inline event handlers.\n- All required IDs and exact text behavior are preserved.\n- Styling does not override required IDs, text or behavior.",
